  {
    "episode_id": 70674,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70674.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Oh, listen, there's no question about that. Listen, President Trump is still extremely popular in Georgia, especially among Republican voters and even especially among primary voters in Georgia. I mean, in ballpark of 80 plus percent approval, he is deeply loved and appreciated. And look, I'm in Congress. I was an original member of the House Freedom Caucus. There were Jim Jordan, Mark Meadows and Ron DeSantis down in Florida and a host of others. And we've got a lot of water under the bridge with President Trump during his administration in Washington and you know, for people who may not be familiar with the Freedom Call because we kind of refer to ourselves as the Republican wing of the Republican Party quite frankly. I mean, it's a group of just incredible men and women who run on and do what they ran on, and just an incredible group of champions. But we've developed a tremendously tight relationship as a caucus with President Trump. And yeah, probably within an hour of me announcing that I was running for Secretary of State, he came out immediately. And this was March of last year. He came out immediately with just a glowing endorsement. And yeah, it's been extremely, extremely helpful and I'm deeply grateful for his trust that I'll be able to clean up the mess that we have here at Georgia's election system.",
