  {
    "episode_id": 70674,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70674.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, that's a great question. And you're referring a while ago about some of the things that he did to create a mess of things that should have never been done and with my leadership would not be done. But things like sending out unilaterally, I mean, this was totally his decision, sending out absentee ballot requests to everyone on our voter registration file. Rick, I mean, that's just disastrous. I think he sent out applications to nearly 7 million people and had taken away because of Stacey Abrams, virtually all signature verification of those ballots. So there's basically no voter ID. He sends out these ballot applications to some 7 million people. The big problem with that is our voter registration file is between 8 and 15% inaccurate. We're 10% inaccurate. That means we're in the ballpark of some 700,000 people who receive an application for a ballot who do not belong on our voter files for whatever reasons, small reasons, large reasons, whatever some 700,000 people who should not be offered a ballot, especially one that has no identification. That should never have happened in the drop-off boxes. We saw, and now there's a movie coming out next week about the mules. There were some 242 here in Georgia that had been identified as going from one drop-off box to another, harvesting the likes that we've never seen. So look, these kinds of things, our elections are so critical. these things cannot be permitted to take place.",
