    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, SB 2 is a great step in the right direction. And I would just mind you, also, Brad Raffensberger has been adamant that this was the most secure election in the history of Georgia. If that were the case, which it absolutely was not, there would be no need for SB 202. But this last election was so disastrous, the Georgia General Assembly had to close the gaps, the enormous gaps, that were created by Brad Drafensberger's unilateral decisions to do some of these things that we're talking about right now. So SB 202, great step in the right direction. It does make voting more accessible while making it more difficult to cheat, regardless of what Democrats out there may try to say about it. It's a good step in the right direction. I would prefer that it would eliminate drop-off boxes and some of these other things, but it is a good step in the right direction. I'm very proud of our general assembly for moving in this direction. Hopefully, it will help us as we're coming up to this later. 23 percent, only 23 percent of Georgians feel very confident that this upcoming election is going to be",
