  {
    "episode_id": 70674,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70674.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "Rick, I think that's a great point that you bring out. You know, we had all this, all these accusations and of course the baseball game was moved from Atlanta and all this kind of stuff, all the accusations and it is more accessible to vote in Georgia than even where the in Colorado, where they moved the Alstral game to. So all this stuff, it's just political theater. And I think we all get tired of the political theater. We just want the truth. And we want to deal with the truth when there are problems. Let's fix it. Let's get it right. But quit the political accusations and all the stuff that so frequently is blown out of proportion. It's just not accurate whatsoever. And that's one of them that you're bringing up.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
