  {
    "episode_id": 70674,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70674.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "is hard. If we have fair elections, and my candidate loses okay well i may be upset about that but so long as we have a system that is in fairness then we can work it out and we can get back to the ballot box next time and hopefully we can win again but if ever our election process is compromised to the point that people no longer have confidence that their votes count, then we've got some major problems. And that has happened, and we've got to turn this around. And one of the things, quite frankly, that I've been stunned by this current Secretary of State is the refusal, the unwillingness, seemingly, to go after individuals with criminal prosecution referrals for those who violate our election laws. if there are no consequences for cheating, cheating will continue to take place. We've got to have leadership that will go after people when they do violate our election laws, and let's keep it fair. Let's keep it accurate. But listen, the voice of the people as I referenced a moment ago with the consent of the government. That is just like a heartbeat of mine. That is politically speaking what this country operates off of and at all costs. That ballot box has got to be defended and protected.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
